==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries allows two AuditEntry atoms for the same application to share identical (prevStatus, newStatus) pairs, which models a duplicate/overwritten chain position — exactly what AppendOnly and FR_018_AuditImmutability forbid. The injection forces such a duplicate to exist.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditImmutability
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditImmutability: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfDecision  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfDecision.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoSelfDecision allows a non-initial AuditEntry's actor to equal the application's applicant — i.e., an officer self-approves their own loan. The injection forces this to exist, which NoSelfMutation and FR_013_NoSelfApproval must catch.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_013_NoSelfApproval
      - NoSelfMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_NoSelfApproval: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfAssignment  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfAssignment.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoSelfAssignment allows the assignedOfficer of an application to be the same user as the applicant. The injection forces a self-assigned application into the model, directly violating FR_011_NoSelfAssignment.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_NoSelfAssignment
      - FR_011_NoSelfAssignment: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly allows a non-auditor (e.g., an officer or applicant) to issue a GetAuditLog call, violating the audit-endpoint auditor-only restriction and the NoInformationLeakage invariant. The injection forces such a call to exist.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_RoleMutualExclusion  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_RoleMutualExclusion.als
    rationale: Removing F_RoleMutualExclusion allows a User to simultaneously hold both ROfficer and RAuditor, which is explicitly forbidden by FR-002. The injection creates such a user, which FR_002_RoleMutualExclusion must catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_002_RoleMutualExclusion
      - FR_002_RoleMutualExclusion: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerApplicant  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerApplicant.als
    rationale: Removing F_OneInFlightPerApplicant allows a single applicant to have two in-flight (Pending or UnderReview) applications simultaneously. The injection forces exactly this scenario, which FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant must catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant: FAIL (expected)

